From 2c5529c57cd232c44eaf5016773ca51fe1dee4c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 14:04:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Epic 7B.2: Assignment Foundation (ADR-012)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds Assignment as the authoritative, effective-dated placement of a person
into the organization — the source of truth for org unit and primary manager
over time, superseding the denormalized Employee.department/team/manager/
workLocation fields (retained as legacy, not removed).

- Assignment aggregate + validation + pure effective-date helpers
  (half-open [effectiveFrom, effectiveUntil) windows, overlap detection)
- Schema + migration: composite tenant-scoped FKs to Employee (person,
  manager) and OrgUnit; CHECK constraints (no self-manager, valid window);
  a GIST exclusion constraint enforcing at most one primary assignment in
  force per person at any instant — verified against real Postgres
- Write/read repositories (Prisma + in-memory), event-buffering write
  transaction, and a UnitOfWork committing assignment + audit + outbox
  atomically, mirroring the OrgUnit platform pattern
- AssignmentService: assignPrimary, transfer (end + create, atomically),
  and endAssignment, each validating person/manager/org-unit existence
  in-transaction before hitting the database guards; organization.manage
  gated
- Architecture fitness rules extended for the Assignment write/read
  boundary; a structural test guards a single Assignment aggregate, a
  single overlap implementation, and a single service
- 37 unit tests + 6 real-Postgres integration tests (atomicity, DB-level
  guards, GIST exclusion, tenant isolation, cross-tenant FK rejection)

